The safest review agent never posts a reply.

I built an n8n and Claude workflow to read a customer review, check its risk, then queue a draft or escalate it to the owner.

## The stopping rule is the product

A rating of three or below escalates. So do allegations involving illness, injury, hygiene, discrimination, staff conduct, legal action, chargebacks, regulators or press.

Malformed model output fails closed. The workflow escalates instead of guessing.

## Three runs tested three different boundaries

Three live executions averaged 3.48 seconds from intake to delivered alert.

A five-star review reached the approval queue. A two-star review combining food poisoning with a legal threat reached the owner. A one-star complaint involving a child’s illness reached the owner with no suggested response.

## Logging comes before alerting

Every review enters the database before Telegram sends an alert. A notification failure never erases the source event.

Graph dependencies enforce the order. Canvas position does not.

## The reversible work belongs to automation

The agent handles reading, classification, routing and drafting.

The public reply stays with the person responsible for the business.

The boundary is the product.

Built by handlit.
